.Dd November 4, 2026
.Dt MIRRORQ 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mirrorq
.Nd enqueue URLs into the mirrord background daemon queue
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar config
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Op Fl d Ar dest
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl q
.Op Ar url ...
.Nm
.Op Fl h | Fl v
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
submits one or more URLs into the
.Xr mirrord 1
background queue for automatic downloading.
.Pp
URLs may be passed as positional arguments on the command line,
read from standard input (one URL per line) when standard input is
piped or redirected from a file, or both.
Empty lines and lines beginning with
.Ql #
are ignored.
.Pp
For each URL,
.Xr mirrord 1
automatically detects the appropriate download method
.Pq archiveorg , ftp , git , gopher , groupsio , http , rsync , or sourceforge
and mirrors into the configured destination directory.
If an identical job (same method, source, destination directory, and flags)
already exists in any state (active, queued, or finished), no new job number
is allocated and the existing job is left in its current state unless
.Fl f
is given.
.Pp
The flags are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c , Fl config Ar path
Configuration file to read.
The default is
.Pa ~/.config/mirrortools/config.toml
or
.Ev $MIRROR_CONFIG .
.It Fl s , Fl socket Ar path
Path to the
.Xr mirrord 1
Unix domain socket.
The default is
.Pa $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/mirrortools/mirrord.sock ,
.Pa ~/.local/state/mirrortools/mirrord.sock ,
or
.Ev $MIRRORD_SOCKET .
.It Fl d , Fl dest Ar dir
Override the destination directory for the enqueued jobs.
.It Fl f , Fl force
If an identical finished or paused job already exists, re-queue it under its
existing job number instead of skipping it.
.It Fl q , Fl quiet
Suppress progress and confirmation messages; only errors are printed.
.It Fl v , Fl version
Print the program version and exit.
.It Fl h , Fl help
Print usage information and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Enqueue URLs passed as command-line arguments:
.Pp
.Dl $ mirrorq https://sourceforge.net/projects/fsd-amoeba/ https://archive.org/details/nasa-audio
.Pp
Pipe a file containing a list of URLs (one per line) into
.Nm :
.Pp
.Dl $ cat urls.txt | mirrorq
.Pp
Redirect standard input directly:
.Pp
.Dl $ mirrorq < urls.txt
.Pp
Override destination directory and suppress confirmation output:
.Pp
.Dl $ mirrorq -q -d /mnt/backups/archive https://archive.org/details/nasa-audio
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mirror 1 ,
.Xr mirrord 1
